{"description":"GitHub issue maleolabs/eka-cli#26 (improvement, medium, source: agent, EKA 1.2.0): MCP read tools always return FULL payloads; orientation passes over a mid-sized project cost hundreds of KB of tokens (observed: domain(Architecture) ~169KB, domain(Execution) ~480KB on project anvil with 110 units), while identity + stateVector + relationships cover ~95% of orientation need.\n\nVerified against source:\n- CONFIRMED: CLI has --no-content (cmd/get.go flagGetNoContent applied via Document.StripContent(); cmd/context.go likewise), but MCP `get` and `domain` schemas accept no such parameter and their capability handlers (internal/eka/capability.go Get/Domain, MarshalCompact) always emit full Document.Content.\n- PARTIAL: the MCP `context` tool on branch feat/sto-mcp-capability-expansion ALREADY exposes noContent (schema lines ~350-353, decoded to contexts.Options.NoContent) - the parity gap is limited to `get` and `domain`.\n- The stripping primitive already exists and is exported: (*machine.Document).StripContent() in eka-core/machine/document.go.\n\nFix direction: add noContent boolean to get/domain tool schemas and forward to StripContent at parity with the CLI. Reporter's stronger suggestion (default domain collections to identity-only summaries) is a breaking change - defer behind an opt-in parameter first; reconsider flipping the default only in a major version.","acceptanceCriteria":"- MCP `get` and `domain` tools accept a `noContent: boolean` parameter; when set, response documents have content stripped via machine.Document.StripContent() (eka-core/machine/document.go).\n- Default behavior unchanged (full payloads) - no breaking change to existing clients; identity-only default for domain listings explicitly deferred.\n- Tool descriptions updated so agents discover the parameter without reading source.\n- Measured before/after payload size on a mid-sized project (e.g. anvil, 110 units): domain listing drops from hundreds of KB to KB-scale with noContent=true.\n- Tests cover stripped responses for both tools (content absent, identity/stateVector/relationships intact).\n- Review findings posted as a comment on maleolabs/eka-cli#26; issue closed only after the fix ships in a release."}